                                                "sense_id": "09a30c61-8d46-3289-9c3e-1c570c432d94",
                                                "text": "The ABC's alphabeticalness doubtless had some attraction for Chaucer, independent of its subject."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da7253b8-68ea-472a-ae6e-9aeb3786878c",
                                                "sense_id": "09a30c61-8d46-3289-9c3e-1c570c432d94",
                                                "text": "The alphabeticalness is important because it's simple and because the words a poet writes are things made of alphabet elements where vowels are the sounding spaces."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "08ef54e1-23b7-4a2e-a0f3-dae229d05486",
                                                "sense_id": "09a30c61-8d46-3289-9c3e-1c570c432d94",
                                                "text": "There seems to be even a fourth reason for not adhering to strict alphabeticalness: 9.4. Keep combinations that are closely related in meaning together by entering them in the entry for the first element Thus, e.g. the OALD says in[…]"
